{"id":"diagram-revision-56b29510-a76d-4759-968f-0e542c10d698","diagramId":"diagram-5d2bc009-df74-4f64-a3d4-75d756b9582f","parentId":"diagram-revision-a849b15f-57a6-426b-92dc-62e17d22034e","diagram":{"id":"overview","revision":2,"diagramId":"diagram-5d2bc009-df74-4f64-a3d4-75d756b9582f","revisionId":"diagram-revision-56b29510-a76d-4759-968f-0e542c10d698","content":{"revisionId":"overview:2","ascii":"Saved CanvasViews and branching\n|\n+-- A named view remembers a saved state; editing can move beyond it\n|   +-- CREATE names the current canvas and makes that view active\n|   |   `-- The first checkpoint is also its initial saved endpoint\n|   +-- SAVE advances the active view's saved endpoint\n|   |   +-- Keep earlier checkpoints; add the current checkpoint if new\n|   |   `-- Clear the saved view's stashed working copy\n|   `-- Unsaved means different from that endpoint\n|       `-- Camera and selection alone do not mark the view dirty\n|\n+-- Ownership: the canvas history owns the records that views refer to\n|   +-- CanvasHistory.record\n|   |   +-- canvasViews: names, branch links, active view and working copies\n|   |   |   +-- Each saved view refers to its first and latest saved checkpoints\n|   |   |   |   `-- startCheckpointId / finalCheckpointId / checkpointIds\n|   |   |   `-- workingCopies[viewId] -> checkpoint to resume after switching\n|   |   +-- snapshots: stored canvas composition and view state\n|   |   |   `-- diagramBindings -> exact revisions in diagramRevisions\n|   |   `-- diagramRevisions: shared revision records, held separately\n|   `-- Saving or branching retains existing saved checkpoints\n|       `-- A child can share its starting state without sharing future edits\n|\n+-- Calls: opening another view protects the work being left behind\n|   `-- CanvasViewControls.command -> onCommand(request)\n|       `-- CanvasViewReceiver.apply -> controller.canvasView\n|           +-- Receiver retains a request receipt, then invokes persistence\n|           |   `-- Retrying the same request saves without applying it twice\n|           `-- CanvasHistory.canvasView dispatches the requested operation\n|               `-- OPEN invokes openCanvasView\n|                   +-- Select the target's working copy, or its saved endpoint\n|                   +-- Invoke stashCanvasView for the outgoing view\n|                   |   `-- Remember its current checkpoint, including unsaved work\n|                   `-- Restore the target as a fresh current checkpoint\n|                       +-- Keep the current camera in place\n|                       `-- Reopening resumes edits; SAVE makes them the endpoint\n|\n+-- Ancestry: a branch starts from an explicit saved parent checkpoint\n|   +-- FORK creates one child, then invokes the same opening path above\n|   |   `-- Unsaved parent edits stay with the parent; save first to include them\n|   +-- ALTERNATIVES creates independent children from one pinned checkpoint\n|   |   +-- The current canvas stays open; this operation only creates copies\n|   |   `-- All children share a group, then develop independently\n|   `-- Each child's links answer different questions\n|       +-- parentViewId -> which view this child descended from\n|       |   `-- Following parent links reveals the branch's ancestry\n|       +-- forkCheckpointId -> which exact parent state it started from\n|       `-- alternativeGroupId -> which candidates belong to one choice\n|           `-- KEEP the chosen candidate\n|               +-- Open/resume it if needed, then save its current state\n|               `-- Archive the other group members\n|                   `-- Also archive every descendant of those other branches\n|\n+-- DISCARD archives a branch and every descendant\n|   +-- If the active view is inside that branch\n|   |   +-- Open the discarded branch root's parent when available\n|   |   `-- Otherwise stash the current state and clear the active view\n|   `-- Archived views leave the explorer; their saved history is retained\n|\n`-- Data dependencies cross these branches: an arrow means \"needs\"\n    +-- Restored canvas -> chosen checkpoint -> composition + bound revisions\n    |   `-- documentFromHistory resolves bindings to reconstruct the document\n    +-- Dirty indicator -> current state + active view's saved endpoint\n    +-- New child -> parent's saved endpoint, independent of its working copy\n    `-- Archive set -> chosen group or discarded root + descendant links\n        `-- These dependencies describe required inputs, not ownership or calls","asciiSha256":"36ad02a18437180bf4abe22b6263b4759db5eaf3fb1ec3d3d744dd4ffd1be44b","structure":{"kind":"tree","parserVersion":"ascii-tree-2","rootIds":["overview:2:36ad02a18437180bf4abe22b6263b4759db5eaf3fb1ec3d3d744dd4ffd1be44b:line-1"],"nodes":{"overview:2:36ad02a18437180bf4abe22b6263b4759db5eaf3fb1ec3d3d744dd4ffd1be44b:line-1":{"id":"overview:2:36ad02a18437180bf4abe22b6263b4759db5eaf3fb1ec3d3d744dd4ffd1be44b:line-1","label":"Saved CanvasViews and branching","line":1,"branchColumn":-1,"startColumn":1,"endColumn":31,"childIds":["overview:2:36ad02a18437180bf4abe22b6263b4759db5eaf3fb1ec3d3d744dd4ffd1be44b:line-3","overview:2:36ad02a18437180bf4abe22b6263b4759db5eaf3fb1ec3d3d744dd4ffd1be44b:line-12","overview:2:36ad02a18437180bf4abe22b6263b4759db5eaf3fb1ec3d3d744dd4ffd1be44b:line-24","overview:2:36ad02a18437180bf4abe22b6263b4759db5eaf3fb1ec3d3d744dd4ffd1be44b:line-38","overview:2:36ad02a18437180bf4abe22b6263b4759db5eaf3fb1ec3d3d744dd4ffd1be44b:line-54","overview:2:36ad02a18437180bf4abe22b6263b4759db5eaf3fb1ec3d3d744dd4ffd1be44b:line-60"],"foldRanges":[{"startLine":2,"endLine":66}]},"overview:2:36ad02a18437180bf4abe22b6263b4759db5eaf3fb1ec3d3d744dd4ffd1be44b:line-3":{"id":"overview:2:36ad02a18437180bf4abe22b6263b4759db5eaf3fb1ec3d3d744dd4ffd1be44b:line-3","label":"A named view remembers a saved state; editing can move beyond it","line":3,"branchColumn":0,"startColumn":5,"endColumn":68,"parentId":"overview:2:36ad02a18437180bf4